      {
        "id": 163655,
        "name": "JimmyTheCannon",
        "username": "JimmyTheCannon",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/cdc98d/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-03-01T17:04:32.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Jgraygaming2\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/34f0e0/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Jgraygaming2:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Thus far, the Sentinels community has been mostly polite but I’m alway wary of voice chat based on my (admitedly) limited MMO experience. I do not want:1. To hear people eating.2. To hear their music instead of the game’s.3. To hear their conversation with their parent/friend/sibling.4. Listen to their homophobic or misogynistic slurs.5. Listen to their lack of imagination in the use of adjectives (there ARE other adjectives besides variations of the ‘f’ word).Really, my experience with voice chat and games has just made me shudder.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Simple solution to most of that is for the voice chat to be push-to-talk.</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:44:42.891Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
