      {
        "id": 163657,
        "name": "JimmyTheCannon",
        "username": "JimmyTheCannon",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/cdc98d/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-03-01T17:45:41.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Matchstickman\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/48/1880_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Matchstickman:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I hate push to talk, because it is almost always push-and-hold to talk, and I am doing other things that require hands while talking.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>While playing Sentinels? It’s completely mouse-driven.</p>\n<p>I use Mumble or TeamSpeak for various online games - my PTT key is left alt. With most games I can push that and talk without it interfering with the game at all.</p>",
